{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"signal r signal r","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md","fileName":"SignalR.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SignalR","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Real-Time Web Communication]] [[Azure SignalR Service Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","Azure SignalR Service Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"signal r signal r","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR.md","fileName":"SignalR.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SignalR","heading":"SignalR","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"SignalR is an ASP.NET Core library for real-time communication between server code and connected clients. Unlike a REST exchange initiated only by the client, it lets the server send a message when an event occurs.\n\nA server exposes a hub and a React client creates a hub connection with named message handlers. This supplements rather than replaces REST: commands and resource retrieval can remain HTTP operations while notifications travel over the live connection.\n\nThe Azure chat project separates SignalR's programming model from its hosting infrastructure. The application still defines a hub and named client callbacks, while Azure SignalR Service manages the scalable connection layer used to broadcast chat and archive notifications.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","Azure SignalR Service Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":